    <string name="privacy_intro">Below is what apps can access, based on permissions reported by Android. A granted permission does not mean an app is dangerous — it may be needed for a feature. You can change it in settings at any time.</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_text">PHONEBOOST needs no account and does not send your personal data to any server. Device readings, the app list and permissions are read on your phone only. Access to photos and videos is requested only when you tap “Find large files”. Check history is stored only in your phone’s internal storage. If you turn on the optional “Automation”, background diagnostics and (with permission) notifications run; a PDF report leaves the phone only if you save or share it.</string>
